<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baltic Landeswehr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Baltische Landeswehr</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Baltic Landeswehr was a volunteer force formed in Latvia in late 1918, mainly from Baltic German nobles and townspeople, with Latvian and Russian units. Fighting alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freikorps">German Freikorps</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolsheviks">Bolsheviks</a>, it recaptured Riga in May 1919. It was defeated by Estonian and Latvian forces at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesis">Cēsis</a> in June 1919 and was then reorganised under British supervision as part of the Latvian army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baltic-landeswehr.jpg" alt="Baltic Landeswehr" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Graphic made by Carport · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Baltic_Germans.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…aided by Finnish volunteers and a British naval squadron, drove the invaders out by early 1919, defeated the <b>Baltic German Landeswehr</b> at the Battle of Cēsis in June 1919, and fought on until Soviet Russia recognised Estonian independence in perpetuity by the Treaty of Tartu on 2 February…</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Republic of Estonia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Latvian and Estonian troops defeated the German <b>Landeswehr</b> at the Battle of Cēsis in June 1919, the national government returned to Riga, and the attack of Pavel Bermondt-Avalov's West Russian Volunteer Army on the capital was repulsed in November.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-latvia">Republic of Latvia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>German Freikorps and the <b>Baltic Landeswehr</b>, with Latvian national units, recaptured Riga on 22 May 1919.</blockquote><a href="/state/latvian-socialist-soviet-republic">Latvian Socialist Soviet Republic</a></li><li><blockquote>Baltic German volunteers later fought in the <b>Landeswehr</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/united-baltic-duchy">United Baltic Duchy</a></li></ul></section>
